# SPECIMEN: which combination lets a mod carry its OWN art?
#
# On engine 1.3.4 nothing did. `artfileroot` resolves relative to `data/graphics/ships` and
# will not walk out of it - measured here, bracketed by controls.
#
# Engine 1.3.5 added two things that change the question:
#   sbs.add_extra_ship_data(file, path)  loads ship data straight out of a mod folder.
#                                        MEASURED WORKING: the engine read shields [110,90]
#                                        from anime_ships/mod_ships.json with nothing
#                                        written into the mission.
#   art_file_path                        a PATH sibling to the name-based artfileroot,
#                                        available on hullmap AND in ship data files.
#
# So the data half is solved and only the ART half is open: WHICH combination of the two
# fields, and which spelling of the path, does the engine honor? Each variant changes
# exactly one thing, and they are judged side by side in a single frame - nine ships is a
# lot, but one look settles what would otherwise be ten engine runs. The path spellings
# cover absolute plus every plausible ROOT a relative one could be resolved against:
# data/graphics/ships, the mission folder, data/, and the exe folder.
#
# READ THEM BY NAME, NEVER BY SIDE. The frame is mirrored in world X: the ship at the
# lowest x draws on the RIGHT. An earlier version of this card said LEFT/RIGHT and the
# first engine look read as a contradiction until the controls settled it. Every ship is
# name-tagged; judge by the tag.
#
#     modart_control_ok    must be a real TSN hull      - the frame is working
#     modart_control_bad   must be the placeholder      - failure is visible
#     everything between   God Phoenix = that spelling WORKS
#
# If the two controls look alike, the specimen is broken and nothing between them counts.

@map/visual_mod_art "Visual: mod-carried art"
" Which artfileroot / art_file_path combination reaches a mod's own meshes?
    visual_set_index_by_name("mod_art")
    await task_schedule(run_visual_mod_art)
    ->END


=== run_visual_mod_art
metadata: ``` yaml
type: visual/mod_art
```
    # Built and loaded HERE rather than at story top level. add_extra_ship_data takes a
    # path and is documented "just for this mission", and it was measured working when
    # called after sim_create - unlike extraShipData.json, which must be on disk before
    # create_new_sim() reads it. The variants carry absolute paths, so the file is
    # generated at run time: an absolute path committed to a repo is wrong on every other
    # machine.
    _loaded, _note = mod_art_build_and_load()

    _keys = mod_art_variant_keys()
    _gap = 1100
    _made = 0
    _x0 = 0 - (len(_keys) - 1) * _gap / 2
    for _vi in range(len(_keys)):
        # Breadcrumb BEFORE the spawn: one of these variants asserts the engine, and an
        # assert writes no report, so the last line in mod_art_progress.txt is the culprit.
        mod_art_mark("SPAWNING", _keys[_vi])
        _o = npc_spawn(_x0 + _vi * _gap, 0, 0, _keys[_vi], "tsn", _keys[_vi], "behav_npcship")
        if _o is not None:
            _made += 1
        mod_art_mark("SPAWNED", _keys[_vi])

    mod_art_mark("SURVIVED ALL SPAWNS")
    _anchor = visual_anchor(0, 0, 0)
    # One ship gets a tight frame; a row of them needs the wide one. Nothing subtle here -
    # the wide lens makes a single hull a speck, which is exactly what "it is a bit small"
    # meant the first time this was looked at.
    if len(_keys) == 1:
        visual_camera(_anchor, lens=(0, 60, -260))
    else:
        visual_camera(_anchor, lens=(0, 1600, -5800))

    _expect = ~~[
        "TEN ships in a row - read them by NAME, the frame is mirrored in X",
        "modart_control_ok is a real TSN hull",
        "modart_control_bad is the placeholder sphere",
        "those two must LOOK DIFFERENT, or nothing between them counts",
        "any variant drawn as a God Phoenix is a spelling that WORKS",
        "1.3.4 measured: none worked. 1.3.5 added add_extra_ship_data and art_file_path.",
    ]~~
    visual_case("Mod-carried art: which combination", _expect,
        notes="absolute, and relative to graphics/ships, mission, data, exe",
        data=f"{_made} of {len(_keys)} spawned - {_note}")

    # The data half can only confirm the ships exist and the loader took. It cannot see
    # art, which is the entire reason this is a specimen and not a headless probe.
    visual_expect("mod art: variants loaded", _loaded, _note)
    visual_expect("mod art: all variants spawned", _made == len(_keys), f"{_made}/{len(_keys)}")
    ->END
